From: TDVP maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] pkg_hash: preserve file records when owner is unchanged

list-upgradable initializes the file ownership hash twice. Reassigning a
file to the same package must not remove its installed file record: the
caller still uses that record while walking the installed file list.
Otherwise pkg_info_preinstall_check accesses freed memory on the second
pass. Offline-root tests can mask this because the stripped lookup path
does not match the absolute path stored in the file list.

Keep the existing ownership-transfer behavior for different packages.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
+++ b/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
@@ -918,6 +918,9 @@ void file_hash_set_file_owner(const char *file_name, pkg_t * owning_pkg)
     file_name = strip_offline_root(file_name);
 
     old_owning_pkg = hash_table_get(&opkg_config->file_hash, file_name);
+    if (old_owning_pkg == owning_pkg)
+        return;
+
     hash_table_insert(&opkg_config->file_hash, file_name, owning_pkg);
 
     /*
